SUMMARY:Deadline: Trusted Creator Fellowship 2026 (News Creator Corps)
DESCRIPTION:A short-term virtual fellowship from News Creator Corps that tr
 ains independent content creators in the tactical craft of journalism: fac
 t-checking\, sourcing and interviewing\, applied directly to their own cha
 nnels during the programme so the community they already serve gets more c
 redible information. WHO IT IS FOR: independent creators with an engaged f
 ollowing on digital platforms (Instagram\, TikTok\, Twitch\, Substack\, Yo
 uTube and similar) whose content is information-based and serves a specifi
 c community. It is explicitly not aimed at traditional journalists already
  trained in reporting fundamentals. STUDENT SEATS: three places in the aut
 umn cohort are reserved for full-time college students aged 25 or younger\
 , who get the same fellowship experience as everyone else. WHAT FELLOWS RE
 CEIVE: a $5\,000 stipend on completion\, weekly virtual sessions\, and acc
 ess to discussion forums with the cohort\, trainers\, staff and alumni. EL
 IGIBILITY: US-based only. KEY DATES: applications close 17 August 2026 at 
 11:59pm ET\; notifications by the end of September 2026\; programme runs r
 oughly 5 October to 18 December 2026. Contact: creatorprogram@newscreatorc
 orps.org. Sibling programme to the Rural Creator Fellowship.\n\nOrganisati
 on: News Creator Corps (a project of the Good Information Foundation)\nLoc
 ation: Virtual\, meeting once a week. RESTRICTED: US-based creators only.\
 nAward: $5\,000 stipend on completing the programme. No application fee.\n
 Duration: Roughly 5 October to 18 December 2026\, virtual sessions once a 
 week\n\nMore: https://newscreatorcorps.org/programs/trusted-creator/apply/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://newscreatorcorps.org/programs/trusted-creator/apply/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Virtual\, meeting once a week. RESTRICTED: US-based creators only.
END:VEVENT
